{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On this [D]road I [G]walk a[D]long,
Seasons dim and [G]seasons [D]dawn
And the [Bm]years keep [A]rambling [G]on.
They ramble [D]on.
I know well this [G]world I [D]see,
Shared with friends and [G]fami[D]ly,
But a [Bm]voice keeps [A]telling [G]me
I'm sick for [D]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Jesus, [G]only [A]You can [Dadd2]satis[D]fy.
[D/F#]You a[G]lone make [A]all things [Bm]new.
[A]You're the [G]Way, the [A]Truth, the [F#m7]Life and [Bm7]I'm,
Oh I'm, [G]coming [A]home to [D]You.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]The rugged cross that [G]Jesus [D]bore
Draws my thoughts towards [G]Heaven's [D]shore
Where the [Bm]One I'm [A]living [G]for
Prepares my [D]home.
[D]Lord, the beauty [G]of your [D]grace
And the promise [G]of your [D]face
Bid me [Bm]make this [A]world a [G]better place
Until I'm [D]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
[D]Jesus, [G]only [A]You can [Dadd2]satis[D]fy.
[D/F#]You a[G]lone make [A]all things [Bm]new.
[A]You're the [G]Way, the [A]Truth, the [F#m7]Life and [Bm7]I'm,
Oh I'm, [G]coming [A]home to [G]You.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Tag}
I'm coming home!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 3}
[A]Jesus, [G]only [A]You can [Dadd2]satis[D]fy.
[D/F#]You a[G]lone make [A]all things [Bm]new.
[A]You're the [G]Way, the [A]Truth, the [F#m7]Life and [Bm7]I'm,
Oh I'm, [G]coming [A]home to [Bm]You.
Lord, I'm [G]coming [A]home to [D]You.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]When my final [G]day is [D]done
And this earthly [G]race is [D]run,
I will [Bm]bow be[A]fore the [G]One
Who calls me [D]home.
[D]Yes I'll [Bm]bow be[A]fore the [G]One
Who calls me [D]home.
{end_of_verse}
